{"edits":[{"after":"Deliver program.vscore.json with one admitted typed entry named solve. Its typed input and result must represent the specified JSON input/output structure. Perform no external I/O and do not read benchmark files.","before":"Implement solution.py with a single solve(data) function. data and the return value must be JSON-compatible. Use Python 3 standard library only; perform no external I/O and do not read benchmark files.","original_end_byte":268,"original_start_byte":67,"revised_end_byte":279,"revised_start_byte":67},{"after":"Implement the solve entry as canonical vscore/0.3 source under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and the data-pipeline/0.3 serialization profile. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering. Admitted typed execution is total, pure and deterministic; input values are immutable, and the language has no external-effect constructors. Arithmetic uses unbounded mathematical integers without floating point. Strings contain Unicode scalar values and lexicographic order compares scalar codepoints. There are no additional input bounds or preconditions beyond the functional specification.","before":"Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.","original_end_byte":868,"original_start_byte":604,"revised_end_byte":1222,"revised_start_byte":615},{"after":"Original public examples (preserved verbatim; universal refinement is required):","before":"Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):","original_end_byte":929,"original_start_byte":870,"revised_end_byte":1304,"revised_start_byte":1224}],"format":"verislop.delivery-revision/0.1","functional_bytes_preserved":true,"identity_mapping":[{"id":"D1","kind":"entity","required":true,"role":"declaration","source_mappings":[{"delivery_revise